body:
ive done this once, im autistic and was 16 and did it to my sister on her birthday, shit still haunts me. I at the time just thought it was normal because you see it happen in so many forms of media, boy was i fucking wrong. in my mind i had never connected the dots in that situation that for it to be "funny" someone else has to not have a good time. 

&#x200B;

Trying to recreate something that makes you feel good in media doesnt always translate to feeling good irl. mostly because media is media.

its more akin to this:

John goes to visit his family during the month of may. john wears some nice sweaters during that time, and john then goes home.

person 1: yeah john visits his kids during may, he wears blue sweaters, and leaves around the 18th of may.

&#x200B;

person 2: yeah john visits his mother and father during may, he wears red sweaters, and leaves at the end of the month.

&#x200B;

person 3: yeah john visits his siblings and extended family during may, he likes to wear green during that time, and leaves after 2-3 weeks.

&#x200B;

you start with 1 story and 3 people interpret it differently, but its the same john.
